{
  "case_id": "2017-16-1150",
  "document_hash": "12d949bb6519a99951610d9b845f0e29d8335d8eb9e5ac9056f2a481a2f748ae",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1150",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "12d949bb6519a99951610d9b845f0e29d8335d8eb9e5ac9056f2a481a2f748ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-12d949bb6519-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ANDREW C. SIMPSON, Christiansted, V.I.; on behalf of the Petitioner.\nNEAL K. KATYAL, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Respondents."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1150",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "12d949bb6519a99951610d9b845f0e29d8335d8eb9e5ac9056f2a481a2f748ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-12d949bb6519-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SIMPSON: Mr. Chief Justice, may it please the Court:\nEver since the Judiciary Act of 1789,\nthere has been a right of appeal from a final\njudgment. We ask that this Court support the\nright of appeal in this case because -- for\nthree reasons.\nFirst, it comes from a final judgment\nentered in the case. It provides a bright-line\nrule that brooks no exception. When a final\njudgment is entered, you have a right of\nappeal."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1150",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "12d949bb6519a99951610d9b845f0e29d8335d8eb9e5ac9056f2a481a2f748ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-12d949bb6519-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Please explain to\nme what the purpose of 42 -- dividing it up\ninto two sections is."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1150",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "12d949bb6519a99951610d9b845f0e29d8335d8eb9e5ac9056f2a481a2f748ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-12d949bb6519-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SIMPSON: Certain -- certainly."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1150",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "12d949bb6519a99951610d9b845f0e29d8335d8eb9e5ac9056f2a481a2f748ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-12d949bb6519-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: I don't understand\nthe necessity, meaning if we had only (a)(1),\nthe court could do exactly what you're saying\nas well. It didn't need (a)(2) to accomplish\nwhat (a)(1) already says it can. It suggests to me that there's a separate purpose for\n(a)(2)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1150",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "12d949bb6519a99951610d9b845f0e29d8335d8eb9e5ac9056f2a481a2f748ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-12d949bb6519-0000-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Your -- your client\nhas not brought a lawsuit with multiple claims.\nYour client has brought a claim. And it's not like a -- one plaintiff has one, two, three\nclaims. This is a separate claim brought not\nby the plaintiff, so it's not the plaintiff\npicking one claim and -- and leaving out\nanother plaintiff's claim."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1150",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "12d949bb6519a99951610d9b845f0e29d8335d8eb9e5ac9056f2a481a2f748ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-12d949bb6519-0000-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Mr. Simpson, I guess I\ndon't understand your answer to Justice\nSotomayor or Justice Ginsburg because, although\nthis suit does present this different kind of\nissue, I took it that your argument would apply\njust as well to a suit in which somebody has\nfive claims, splits them up into five different\nlawsuits."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1150",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "12d949bb6519a99951610d9b845f0e29d8335d8eb9e5ac9056f2a481a2f748ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-12d949bb6519-0000-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SIMPSON: Absolutely. And that's why I say that if -- if that case that Justice\nKagan has described gets to that point, then,\nyes, they must appeal, and then I think the\ncourt of appeals has the ability to look at\nthem and say, well, this case should have been\nbrought as one case and I'm going to -- the\ncourt can say I will stay that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1150",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "12d949bb6519a99951610d9b845f0e29d8335d8eb9e5ac9056f2a481a2f748ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-12d949bb6519-0000-0010",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the amici, but I think if you look at the\narchitecture of the rules, again, Rule 23(f)\nalso deals with an appeal coming up,\nan interlocutory appeal under the class action\nstatutes, and there the discretion is given\ncompletely to the appellate court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1150",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "12d949bb6519a99951610d9b845f0e29d8335d8eb9e5ac9056f2a481a2f748ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-12d949bb6519-0000-0015",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 17,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Suppose you were\narguing this point before the civil rules\ncommittee, and so the question would be: What\nis the best procedure? What would your\nargument be? Why is the procedure you outline\na better one than the alternative?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1150",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "12d949bb6519a99951610d9b845f0e29d8335d8eb9e5ac9056f2a481a2f748ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-12d949bb6519-0000-0019",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: So -- and it's not\njust laymen, right? I mean, if you look at\nBlack's Law Dictionary, it says a consolidation\nin civil procedure, it defines as \"the\ncourt-ordered unification of two or more\nactions into a single action.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1150",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "12d949bb6519a99951610d9b845f0e29d8335d8eb9e5ac9056f2a481a2f748ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-12d949bb6519-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In which case I have just one question, which is forget the consolidation for a moment, just to clarify in my mind; think of Rule 54(b), imagine it's a case with a lot of parties and a lot of issues, and Rule 54(b), I think, says that \"the court can direct entry of a final judgment as to one or more, but fewer than all, the claims or parties,\" right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Katyal",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1150",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "12d949bb6519a99951610d9b845f0e29d8335d8eb9e5ac9056f2a481a2f748ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-12d949bb6519-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The district here entered -- the court entered an order here consolidating for all purposes the cases brought by brother and sister against each other. Instead of challenging that, Petitioner wants to appeal part of its claims now."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice SOTOMAYOR",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1150",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "12d949bb6519a99951610d9b845f0e29d8335d8eb9e5ac9056f2a481a2f748ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-12d949bb6519-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Could you tell me how you square this with the fact that the district court denied the motion for attorneys' fees because it wasn't filed with -- within 15 days of the final judgment?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1150",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "12d949bb6519a99951610d9b845f0e29d8335d8eb9e5ac9056f2a481a2f748ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-12d949bb6519-0001-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "When an action presents more than one claim for relief -- whether there's a claim, counterclaim, crossclaim, or third-party claim -- or when multiple parties are involved, the court may direct entry of a final judgment as to one or more, but fewer than all."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1150",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "12d949bb6519a99951610d9b845f0e29d8335d8eb9e5ac9056f2a481a2f748ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-12d949bb6519-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Can I ask you, this relates to the question that the Chief asked, and I think it's key: She's lost the case, and"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1150",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "12d949bb6519a99951610d9b845f0e29d8335d8eb9e5ac9056f2a481a2f748ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-12d949bb6519-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: How much time?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1150",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "12d949bb6519a99951610d9b845f0e29d8335d8eb9e5ac9056f2a481a2f748ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-12d949bb6519-0002-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the judge orders a new trial of the other case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. SIMPSON",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1150",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "12d949bb6519a99951610d9b845f0e29d8335d8eb9e5ac9056f2a481a2f748ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-12d949bb6519-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SIMPSON: The -- the characterization of this consolidation changed in the -- from the opposition to the writ for certiorari to the red brief. At the red brief, at the certiorari stage, it was characterized as we did as a consolidation for trial. And that's what it was. I think it's important to understand that all the circuits disagree about even what is consolidation for all purposes. The Bogosian case from the Third Circuit says a case consolidated for pretrial and trial purposes is for all purposes. That's what happened in our case. It was consolidated for pretrial and trial. And so, under the Third Circuit definition, it is all purposes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Official",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1150",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "12d949bb6519a99951610d9b845f0e29d8335d8eb9e5ac9056f2a481a2f748ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-12d949bb6519-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Official have asserted this -- this as a counterclaim against Elsa in her individual capacity."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1150",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "12d949bb6519a99951610d9b845f0e29d8335d8eb9e5ac9056f2a481a2f748ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-12d949bb6519-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted."
    },
    {
